#!/bin/sh
# Button cheat sheet (Help in the menu).
cat <<'EOF'
  RGOS handheld controls
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  The pad drives the mouse pointer by default (panel shows "mouse").

  D-pad      move the pointer           A   click     B   right-click
  L1 / R1    scroll up / down           X   middle-click
  L2 / R2    previous / next window     Y   Esc
  START      main menu (apps, Wi-Fi, power)
  SELECT     on-screen keyboard: d-pad jumps key to key, A types,
             START = Enter, B/SELECT closes it
             (opens by itself for text apps when no USB/BT keyboard
             is attached; plugging one in hides it again)
  MENU tap   pointer -> keys mode (d-pad = arrow keys, A = Enter,
             B = Esc, X = Backspace, Y = Space, L1/R1 = Tab)
  In keys mode MENU closes the focused window; the mouse comes back
  via START -> menu -> Power -> Pointer mode (or MENU held + START).

  MENU held +  B close window      X Wi-Fi        START power menu
               up/down brightness  A Ctrl+C       Y paste
               L1/R1 back/forward  L2/R2 zoom     SELECT game mode
  Game mode gives the pad to games; MENU+SELECT returns.

  Power key: suspend / wake (hold: power off)    Lid: suspend / wake

  Keyboard: Super+Space menu, Super+Enter terminal, Super+E files,
            Super+K keyboard, Alt+Tab switch, Alt+F4 close
  Remap buttons: cp /etc/rgos/padd.conf ~/.config/rgos/
                 then: pkill -HUP rgos-padd
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
EOF
